{
  "id": "guided-participation",
  "term": "guided participation",
  "definition": "Guided participation is a way of learning in which children develop skills by taking part in shared, situation-based activities with adults and peers who shape the interaction and show what counts as appropriate understanding or action. In the source, it refers to children picking up digital literacy abilities through these socially organized exchanges.",
